# Swift Tours — project conventions

## Stack

- Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind, shadcn/ui
- Supabase (Postgres + Auth + Storage)
- Deployed on Vercel

## React

- Default to Server Components. Add `'use client'` only when a component needs browser APIs, WebGL, or event handlers.

## Supabase clients

- Use `@/lib/supabase/server` in Server Components and Route Handlers.
- Use `@/lib/supabase/client` in client components.
- Never import one into the other.
- Never expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` to client code.

## Security

- Security is enforced by Postgres Row Level Security, not by client-side checks.
- Every new table gets RLS policies in the same migration.

## Data & mutations

- Prefer Server Actions over API routes for mutations.
- No `any`. Use the generated Supabase types from `@/types/database.ts` once they exist.

## Code organization

- Keep files focused; extract a component once a file passes ~200 lines.
